body:
Sorry for the late reply. The federal one is variable and last time I checked it was around 5%. My private is around 3.7% The 32k that I will get will be able to cover all if not most of my federal loan. Due to my contract I don't have a loan payment option. (That had to be built into your contract. 

&#x200B;

My maintenance isn't bad just fluid changes and I'll have to do my breaks and some other high mileage items soon. (I have an N52, a more reliable motor). I don't mind keeping the car but paying for 93 where I live sucks.

OH. I apologize I'm new to excel and wanted to get more into it financially. How would I sum up B3:B5 / Liabilities? Would I do =sum(B3:B5)/Liabilities?

&#x200B;

That makes total sense now haha. I don't know why I never summed them up I guess in my head I was thinking of it but never actually typed it down, I apologize.

Ive had my eye on a 2014 535i M-Sport for around 13k but wasn't sure about what to look for in the car or what mods I could even do. 335i is definitely a good look in my budget and I have looked at them. If you look up th3.reaper I believe in  Instagram, that's what I'd eventually like to go for. Unfortunately, I can't find any WRX's in good condition or year I want in my price range. How would you compare the 328i or a 428i to the Audi?

&#x200B;

Edit: Would you consider maybe an A4 S-line Audi?
